This source-only candidate tests the real process_thread_count() in current adopted tests/acceptance-app/main.cpp, 35,921 bytes / SHA256 88b96e34a3509728108ac9504f5e65b905e044852467a0494a8d088a2f65069e. It does not copy the helper or change production source/API. The test TU preincludes all production Windows/SDK/standard headers, then locally redirects the four enumeration/cleanup API calls and renames wWinMain before including that exact main.cpp. Its own wmain calls only the real helper; it never calls the acceptance entry, creates a Host/window or initializes a runtime.

The API wrappers contain fixed thread rows and use the real current PID to exercise filtering. They check TH32CS_SNAPTHREAD/PID0, snapshot identity, initial dwSize and operation counts. Successful CloseHandle deliberately clobbers LastError, so exact saved enumeration diagnostics are meaningful. Every failed call must leave the caller's return sentinel unchanged and close exactly once after a valid snapshot (zero closes after creation failure). Short and oversized First/Next rows stop immediately without a subsequent Next or partial result. Combined enumeration/close and short-row/close failures must retain both diagnostics.

Fifteen named cases cover complete mixed PIDs, empty, foreign-only, the valid minimum owner-field extent, Create/First/Next/Close failure, both enumeration+close double failures, short/oversized First and Next, and Next-short+close double failure. They all expect test exit0 if the helper meets its contract. CTest registers exactly these fifteen, RUN_SERIAL and TIMEOUT30, with no WILL_FAIL. The injected APIs are test observations, not evidence of real OS enumeration, resource trends or fault recovery.

Future Root-only verification: configure separately for Win32 and x64 with fixed v143,version=14.44.35207,host=x64 / SDK19041, an actual normal installed SouiSdk package and explicit absolute SOUI_ACCEPTANCE_MAIN. Target uses console CRT wmain, /MD /U_DEBUG, original inherited diagnostic handles and ordinary installed SDK linkage plus psapi. It needs no Web resources and no runtime binaries because no SDK/Host operation is called. Production SDK TUs, test seam APIs, source overlays and alternate helper implementations are not used. Actual CL.read must include the pinned production main; normal installed archive/headers, actual object/LINK/MAP, fifteen direct/CTest and original strict Owned closure remain for Root's later reviewed execution plan.

No execution packet, future EXE hash or runtime result is supplied. Author performed filesystem/source checks only: no Node, compiler, helper, GUI, VM, Git or live edit. Both architecture results and all broader resource/OS/qualification/release claims remain pending/false. Any future production source change needs a new explicit source pin, not an automatic refresh.
